\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God,labour on; spend, and be spent, 
\par Thy joy to do the Fathers will:
\par It is the way the Master went;
\par Should not the servant tread it still?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Go, labour on; 'tis not for nought,
\par Thy earthly loss is heavenly gain:
\par Men heed thee, love thee, praise thee not;
\par The Master praises; what are men?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Go, labour on, while it is day;
\par The world's dark night is hastening on:
\par Speed, speed thy work, cast sloth away;
\par It is not thus that souls are won.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Men die in darkness at your side,
\par Without a hope to cheer the tomb:
\par Take up the torch, and wave it wide,
\par The torch that lights time's thickest gloom.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Toil on, faint not, keep watch, and pray;
\par Be wise, the erring soul to win;
\par Go forth into the world's highway,
\par Compare the wanderer to come in.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Toil on, and in thy toil rejoice;
\par For toil comes rest, for exile home:
\par Soon shalt thou hear the Bridegroom's voice,
\par The midnight peal: Behold, I come!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

